{
    "map": {
        "description": "Generates an attribute rule specific to symbol rotation logic. The tool outputs a .csv file containing an ArcGIS Arcade attribute rule based on the inputs provided.",
        "field.descr": "The name of an existing field to which the rule will be applied.",
        "field.title": "Rotation Field",
        "in_table.descr": "The point feature class that the new rule will be applied to.",
        "in_table.title": "Input Table",
        "line_classes.descr": "The line feature classes that will be used to intersect the point feature class. The orientation field is a numeric field that is used as a tie breaker when there are multiple intersecting lines.",
        "line_classes.dt.title1": "Line Class",
        "line_classes.dt.title2": "Orientation Field",
        "line_classes.title": "Intersecting Line Classes",
        "out_folder.descr": "<xdoc><p>The folder where the output .csv file will be saved. The name of the file will be the same as the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Table</span> parameter value.</p></xdoc>",
        "out_folder.title": "Output Folder",
        "out_rule_csv.title": "Output CSV File",
        "params.category1": "Options",
        "rotation_options.descr": "<xdoc><p>The rotation options for the point feature class.</p><p>Rotation option components are as follows:<ul><li><span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Point Class Expression</span>—A SQL query that will further limit the features the attribute rule will be applied to. The default is none.</li><li><span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Rotation Style</span>—Specifies how the direction will be measured.<ul><li>Arithmetic—The rotation will start at zero in the east direction and is calculated counterclockwise. This is the default.</li><li>Geographic—The rotation will start at zero in the north direction and is calculated clockwise.</li></ul></li><li><span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Rotate Towards</span>—Specifies whether the feature will be oriented toward the maximum or minimum value.</li><li><ul><li>Minimum—The feature will be oriented toward the minimum value. This is the default.</li><li>Maximum—The feature will be oriented toward the maximum value.</li></ul><span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Additional Rotation</span>—The rotation value that will be added to the calculated rotation value. The default is 0.</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "rotation_options.domain.item2.ARITHMETIC": "Arithmetic",
        "rotation_options.domain.item2.GEOGRAPHIC": "Geographic",
        "rotation_options.domain.item3.MAX": "Maximum",
        "rotation_options.domain.item3.MIN": "Minimum",
        "rotation_options.dt.title1": "Point Class Expression",
        "rotation_options.dt.title2": "Rotation Style",
        "rotation_options.dt.title3": "Rotate Towards",
        "rotation_options.dt.title4": "Additional Rotation",
        "rotation_options.title": "Rotation Options",
        "title": "Generate Symbol Rotation Attribute Rule",
        "where_clause.descr": "A SQL expression that limits the features the attribute rule will be applied to.",
